In fact, every time the game ends the record file is locked, opened,
completely read, and completely rebuilt and then unlocked (excluding
panics, discovery or wizard mode, other equally exceptional
circumstances, and ignoring the VMS edit in place option which doesn't
apply for me anyway). Even if you start the game and immediately #quit
earning you a score of 0, a complete rebuild happens.

Your suggestions forget some of the functionality and options that go
with the scoreboard, which are the (part?) reason a complete read and
rebuild is necessary. One is the Own option to display all of your a
name/uid's scores. Another is the possible need to remove the new
lowest score for a given name/uid & role combo from the scoreboard
which could be at any arbitrary location below where the new score is
inserted. Some other housekeeping of the scoreboard is done as well.


